<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka's April M2 up 8 pct to 261.4 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka's April M2 up 8 pct to 261.4 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's broad money supply, or M2, rose eight percent to 261.4 billion rupees in April this year against 241.9 billion in the same month in 1996, the Central Bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said in its latest economic report that M2 was 260.7 billion rupees in March, 1997.</p>
</text>
